{#- Shared Gate-0 receipt block (ADR-004 of PLAN-latency-worktree-step-preview).
    Single source for the mechanical receipt-emit instruction across all 7 stages.
    Caller sets before {% include %}:
      gate0_heading    — full heading line (## or ### form)
      gate0_stage      — stage name (used for --stage and /hm:<stage>)
      gate0_pass       — text after "**`pass`** — "
      gate0_fail       — text after "**`fail`** — "
      gate0_standalone — bool; append the "<WT> may be undefined" note (true for
                         stages that do NOT engage isolation themselves).
      gate0_extra_note — optional; an extra sentence appended to the guard
                         paragraph (verify uses this for its Gate-0 loop note).
    Inherits is_codex + harness_maker_src_path from the parent stage context.

    PLAN-token-economy-step-pruning Phase 4: in a FUSED command the variant-free prose
    (the `skipped` rule and the guard base) is hoisted to the workflow preamble and
    rendered once. What stays per stage is what IS per stage: the heading, the pass/fail
    criteria, the guard's own variant tails, and the `--stage <stage>` invocation. That
    last one is NOT redundancy — one receipt per stage is the Gate-0 missing-stage
    mechanism (ADR-016, risk R10); collapsing it would make the autoloop driver see
    three stages missing on every iteration. The atomic branch renders byte-identically
    to the pre-Phase-4 output. -#}
